-- title:
--   Annihilator of a torsion point: a left ideal containing rΛ
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order, i.e. contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated. Let $N\in\mathbb{N}$, let $S$ be a commutative ring, and let $E,E'$ be fake elliptic curves of level $N$ over $S$ with $\Lambda$-action, each consisting of a scheme with a structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} S$, a commutative relative group law on its functor of points, the abelian-scheme property bundle, two-dimensional fibres, and an action of $\Lambda$ by endomorphisms over $S$ satisfying the additivity, multiplicativity and trace axioms. Let $\varphi$ be a morphism from the scheme of $E$ to that of $E'$ commuting with the structure morphisms, such that the induced map on $T$-points (for every scheme $T$ and every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} S$) carries the group law of $E$ to that of $E'$, and such that for each $x\in\Lambda$ the composite of the action of $x$ on $E$ with $\varphi$ equals the composite of $\varphi$ with the action of $x$ on $E'$. Let $r\in\mathbb{N}$, let $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ and let $P_0$ be a point of $E$ over $t$ (a morphism $T \to$ the scheme of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} S$) with $r$-fold group-law iterate equal to the unit section. Then there is a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $J$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose elements are exactly those $x$ belonging to $\Lambda$ for which $\varphi$ applied to the translate of $P_0$ by the action of $x$ is the unit section of $E'$ over $t$; moreover $J\subseteq\Lambda$, the element $r\cdot y$ lies in $J$ for every $y\in\Lambda$, and $m x\in J$ for all $m\in\Lambda$, $x\in J$, so that $J$ is a left $\Lambda$-ideal containing $r\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the standard construction of the annihilator ideal of an $r$-torsion point under a $\Lambda$-equivariant homomorphism of fake elliptic curves: the kernel of $\varphi$ on the cyclic subgroup generated by $P_0$ is cut out by a left ideal of the quaternion order lying above $r\Lambda$. It is used in the analysis of Hecke neighbours of fake elliptic curves, and in particular in the proof of [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.iso_of_heckeNeighbour_of_heckeNeighbour_of_ramified`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.iso_of_heckeNeighbour_of_heckeNeighbour_of_ramified).
